  "result": "I added `groupBy` to `src/cli/group-by.ts` and committed it. `npm run fast` passes (biome, boundaries, tsc and 18 tests).\n\n- **Behavior:** it returns a `Map<string, T[]>`. Groups appear in the order their keys are first seen, and items keep input order within each group.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/group-by.test.ts` covers empty input, ordering of keys and items, and that the input isn't mutated. It also checks that a key like `__proto__` works.\n- **Shard weight:** the first `npm run fast` failed because the repo requires every test file to have a weight in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`. I added `'test/cli/group-by.test.ts': 0.1` there. That value is my guess, since the repo only fills in measured weights after CI runs.\n- **Notes:** the plan is in `docs/notes/group-by-plan.md`, with its steps ticked off.\n- **Task id:** you didn't give one, so the commit title has no task id. The repo's rules (KRN-11) ask for one in commit titles, so you may want to amend it.",
